  "annotations": [
    { "id": "studio-note", "x": 0, "y": -170, "w": 520, "page": "page-1", "text": "Studio: Dettivo's structure (sidebar, history, three-pane meetings) on Omarchy's material (monospace, sharp corners, hairlines, one accent). Every colour, size and spacing comes from the theme's colors.toml and shell.toml, so other themes re-skin it; the Home artboard has a theme tweak to try that. Content is illustrative." },
    { "id": "osd-note", "x": 1400, "y": 1700, "w": 420, "page": "page-1", "text": "OSD and bar glyph are the signature. Same QML component hosted by the Omarchy plugin panel on Omarchy, by dettivo-osd elsewhere." },
    { "id": "dir-note", "x": 0, "y": -140, "w": 520, "page": "page-2", "text": "Two directions considered before Studio. A leans terminal-monitor, B leans reading surface. Studio takes B's calm and A's visible state. Pick one here and Home gets rebuilt in that direction." },
    { "id": "round2-note", "x": 0, "y": -170, "w": 560, "page": "page-3", "text": "Round two. First run is three screens (keys, models, try it) that only appear when no model or no bindings exist; everything they do is a config.toml write. Settings routes show the keys they edit. Meetings list and detail complete the meeting loop. States, the hint sheet, a light theme and the icon close the remaining v1 surfaces." },
    { "id": "settings-note", "x": 0, "y": 2860, "w": 520, "page": "page-3", "text": "Settings pattern: three columns, a route list, the content, and a 'this route writes' block at the bottom. General, Polish, Insertion, Meetings and Diagnostics follow the Models and Hotkeys layout exactly." }
  ],
